<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest, required for App Store submission.

  Opening, resizing, cropping, blurring faces, removing backgrounds and reading
  or stripping metadata all happen on the phone and send no picture (PRIVACY.md).
  The face-blur and background-removal models may be DOWNLOADED to the phone;
  no picture goes the other way.

  Updated 2026-11-21: the phone app recognises a suite sign-in. It was
  "Data Not Collected" from 2026-10-20 (no accounts, Docs_UNI_SIM/login-free-plan.md;
  the online backup and the sign-in email and account id it declared went
  then). What it collects now, and only when the
  phone already holds a UNI·SIM session that ANOTHER suite app made (the
  shared Keychain group co.uk.unisim.suite on iOS, the suite's shared sign-in
  on Android):

  - No sign-in of its own. The phone build sets @unisim/sdk's `noAccounts`
    and `signInInTune: false` (src/main.tsx): no Sign in, no account screens,
    no name or email on screen, no "the app was opened" event (there is no
    <UsageTracker />). It reads the session the device holds and follows it.
  - User ID, linked, App Functionality: the account id the session carries,
    which keys the reads and writes below.
  - Other Data Types, linked, App Functionality: Tune this app's choices are
    kept with the account and read back on its other devices, in
    `user_app_prefs`: this app's own colour scheme and language
    in the `tune:images` row (the SDK's TuneSync), the suite-wide colour scheme
    and language in the `suite` row (with the list of suite apps the account
    has used).

  Name and Email Address are not declared: the phone app shows neither (its
  bar has no personal title) and sends neither.

  Nothing else changes: no picture leaves the phone, and no usage count (the
  suite user count, an install id every 45 s, was retired in @unisim/sdk
  0.187.0, and the anonymous daily open count is off under `noAccounts`).
  Nothing is used for tracking. There are no third-party analytics or
  advertising SDKs.

  Required-reason APIs: @capacitor/filesystem reads file creation and
  modification dates (its `stat`), only on files in the app's own container,
  and neither it nor its IONFilesystemLib pod ships a manifest. Capacitor's
  core frameworks carry their own manifests, and @capacitor/share and the
  SDK's UnisimSdk pod use none of the listed APIs.

  Keep this in step with store-assets/data-safety.json, the App Store
  Connect privacy answers (User ID and Other Data Types: linked, not tracking,
  App Functionality; see Docs_UNI_SIM/store-listings/universal-images.md) and PRIVACY.md.
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- @capacitor/filesystem's stat: files in the app container. C617.1. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- The account id a suite session on the phone carries. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeUserID</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- Tune this app settings kept with the account. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherDataTypes</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
